<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block">
  <!--
    CheeseCritic.mml
    Declarative contract for evidence criticism and challenge evaluation.

    A critic score describes criticism under a named scale. It is not a
    truth value, a reward, or execution authority. This document does not
    register a runtime kernel or mutate memory.
  -->

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>CriticReport</mi><mo>=</mo>
      <mo>&#x27E8;</mo><mi>candidateRef</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>evidenceRefs</mi><mo>,</mo>
      <mi>objections</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>counterexamples</mi><mo>,</mo>
      <mi>criticScore</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>scaleRef</mi><mo>,</mo>
      <mi>recommendation</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>provenance</mi><mo>&#x27E9;</mo>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:cheese-critic:v1">CriticReport</csymbol>
        <list><ci>candidateRef</ci><ci>evidenceRefs</ci><ci>objections</ci>
          <ci>counterexamples</ci><ci>criticScore</ci><ci>scaleRef</ci>
          <ci>recommendation</ci><ci>provenance</ci></list>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
A report evaluates a candidate against cited evidence and a declared critic
scale. It preserves objections and counterexamples so later reviewers can
inspect why the report reached its recommendation.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>Critique</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>candidate</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>evidence</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>scale</mi><mo>)</mo>
      <mo>&#x2192;</mo><mi>CriticReport</mi>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:cheese-critic:v1">EvaluateCriticism</csymbol>
        <ci>candidate</ci><ci>evidence</ci><ci>scale</ci><ci>CriticReport</ci>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
Critique may assess source quality, evidence coverage, contradictions,
counterexamples, uncertainty, recency, and calibration. Critic scores must
name their scale and polarity; a high score may mean strong or numerous
criticism, strong criticism quality, or positive review, depending on that
scale. Scores from different scales are not directly comparable.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>CriticScore</mi><mo>&#x2260;</mo><mi>Truth</mi>
      <mspace width="1em"/><mi>CriticScore</mi><mo>&#x2260;</mo><mi>Reward</mi>
      <mspace width="1em"/><mi>CriticScore</mi><mo>&#x2260;</mo><mi>Legality</mi>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:cheese-critic:v1">ScoreSeparation</csymbol>
        <ci>CriticScore</ci><ci>Truth</ci><ci>Reward</ci><ci>Legality</ci>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
Criticism is evidence about a candidate, not a verdict that the candidate is
false or undesirable. High unresolved challenge pressure can prioritize
investigation even when supporting evidence is substantial. Absence of
criticism does not establish truth. XCFE legality remains an independent gate.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>Recommendation</mi><mo>&#x2208;</mo>
      <mo>{</mo><mi>retain</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>investigate</mi><mo>,</mo>
      <mi>verify</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>deprioritize</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>reject</mi><mo>}</mo>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:cheese-critic:v1">CriticRecommendation</csymbol>
        <list><ci>retain</ci><ci>investigate</ci><ci>verify</ci>
          <ci>deprioritize</ci><ci>reject</ci></list>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
Recommendations are advisory outputs. Selection policy may use them with
objective value, evidence strength, information gain, and cost. Rejection,
fact promotion, learned-weight updates, and execution each require their own
authorized policy and provenance-bearing decision.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>DiscussionInput</mi><mo>=</mo>
      <mo>&#x27E8;</mo><mi>observe</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>compare</mi><mo>,</mo>
      <mi>question</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>plan</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>verify</mi><mo>&#x27E9;</mo>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:cheese-critic:v1">DiscussionInput</csymbol>
        <list><ci>observe</ci><ci>compare</ci><ci>question</ci><ci>plan</ci><ci>verify</ci></list>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
A distilled discussion template (data/micronaut/distilled-questions.json) provides
structured critic input. observe → seeds PromptField gramEvidence; compare →
populates evidenceRefs for Critique(); question → contributes QuestionIdentity
records to the DialogueCycle; plan → feeds candidate proposals; verify → maps to
the critic step in DaemonPatterns.DialogueCycle. DiscussionInput carries
provenance=gemma-distill and is treated as candidate evidence; Ch'en verification
and XCFE legality remain independent gates before any fact promotion.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <mspace linebreak="newline"/>

  <semantics>
    <mrow>
      <mi>CriticFeedback</mi><mo>&#x2192;</mo>
      <mi>DialogueCycle</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>critic</mi>
    </mrow>
    <annotation-xml encoding="MathML-Content">
      <apply>
        <csymbol cd="urn:kuhul:cheese-critic:v1">FeedbackArc</csymbol>
        <ci>CriticReport</ci><ci>DialogueCycleCriticStep</ci>
      </apply>
    </annotation-xml>
    <annotation encoding="text/plain">
CriticReport output feeds the critic step of DaemonPatterns.DialogueCycle.
The recommendation field (retain/investigate/verify/deprioritize/reject) is
advisory to the verify step and does not bypass XCFE or authorize execution.
A CriticReport generated from gemma-distill patterns carries provenance=gemma-distill
and enters the same Ch'en verification path as any other candidate before promotion
to fact or topology change. Jyggalag (T=0.00) is the canonical collapse consumer
of a critic-ranked candidate set; it may cite CriticReport.recommendation as
collapse justification, but the Xul commit still requires the full authority path.
    </annotation>
  </semantics>

  <annotation encoding="text/plain">
CheeseCritic contract invariants:
1. Every objection and score is linked to candidate, evidence, scale, and provenance.
2. Critic-score meaning and polarity are explicit; no universal positive/negative interpretation is assumed.
3. Challenge pressure is distinct from evidence strength, truth, utility, reward, and legality.
4. Critique produces reports and recommendations; it does not mutate GramStore or execute candidates.
5. Runtime registration and XCFE policy are required for any operational effect.
6. DiscussionInput (gemma-distill provenance) enters as gramEvidence; it is not a verified critic scale.
7. CriticFeedback to DialogueCycle.critic is advisory; Jyggalag collapse and Xul commit each require their own authority path.
  </annotation>
</math>
